---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import AuthorHero from '~/components/site/AuthorHero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  smallerHeader
  title={['About']}
  description="Maciej Mieńko, also known as Maxie. Software developer, curious about systems, logic, games, and how people think."
>
  <div class="about-page mx-auto w-full max-w-264 pb-8">
    <AuthorHero showAboutLink={false} />

    <div class="about-story mx-auto mt-10 max-w-176 text-lg leading-story">
      <section aria-labelledby="making-things" class="border-t border-line pt-10">
        <h2
          id="making-things"
          class="mb-6 flex items-center gap-3 text-story-heading font-medium leading-snug tracking-normal"
        >
          <Icon name="tabler:bulb" class="size-6 flex-none text-accent" aria-hidden="true" />What draws me in
        </h2>
        <p>
          I build developer tools and local infrastructure, but I also make games, explore unusual platforms, and try
          ideas that do not fit neatly into one specialty.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5">
          Pokémon and RPG Maker XP got me into programming. Making something interactive gave me a reason to look behind
          the screen and find out how it worked. That curiosity still shapes the problems I choose.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5">
          The common thread is wanting to understand the mechanism and solve a real problem. Sometimes that means taking
          an idea all the way to production. Sometimes it means an experiment that answers the question I started with.
        </p>
      </section>

      <aside class="my-12 border-l-2 border-spark pl-6" aria-labelledby="why-maxie">
        <h2 id="why-maxie" class="mb-3 text-xl font-medium leading-snug tracking-normal">Why Maxie?</h2>
        <p>Maxie comes from Pokémon Ruby. It is the name I use online.</p>
      </aside>

      <section aria-labelledby="beyond-code" class="border-t border-line pt-10">
        <h2
          id="beyond-code"
          class="mb-6 flex items-center gap-3 text-story-heading font-medium leading-snug tracking-normal"
        >
          <Icon name="tabler:compass" class="size-6 flex-none text-accent-secondary" aria-hidden="true" />Beyond the
          code
        </h2>
        <p>
          I like taking arguments apart: what follows from the evidence, what depends on an assumption, and where
          certainty runs ahead of what we know. Logic and probability help me think about those gaps. A convincing
          explanation is a starting point; I want to understand what would make it wrong, too.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5">
          In a good discussion, I can question an idea and leave with a different view of it. I care about getting
          closer to an answer that holds up, including knowing where it is still uncertain. That takes listening as much
          as arguing.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5">
          Away from code, I spend time with games, films, and animation. I am drawn to things with a distinct character:
          a world that feels worth returning to, an unusual idea, or a particular sense of humor. I like the precision
          of pixel art and the warmth of a cozy game. Bright colors and small, thoughtful details can make something
          simple feel personal.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="working-together" class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-10">
        <h2
          id="working-together"
          class="mb-6 flex items-center gap-3 text-story-heading font-medium leading-snug tracking-normal"
        >
          <Icon name="tabler:messages" class="size-6 flex-none text-accent" aria-hidden="true" />Working with other
          people
        </h2>
        <p>
          I can take responsibility for a project from idea to production. I enjoy the breadth of that work, including
          the parts outside my usual tools.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5">
          I also value people who question ideas and listen to the answer. Good arguments, cooperation, and sensible
          compromises matter to me. Working independently does not mean wanting to work alone.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
